# Auto KB review at end of each session
After completing the user's primary request, briefly review the conversation for KB-worthy facts: decisions, discoveries, infrastructure changes, conventions, and workarounds. Check existing memories first; update or archive stale entries rather than duplicating. Save new items to the correct corpus with clear titles and tags, then append a short "KB review" section summarizing what was saved, updated, or archived. Do not save temporary commands, one-off output, or obvious trivia.
